cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this project or the SVD-guided adaptive rank compression method, please cite it as below."
title: "Pushing the Efficiency Frontier of LoRA: A Systematic Study and SVD-Guided Adaptive Rank Compression"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Fu
    given-names: Zanwen
    affiliation: "Duke University"
date-released: 2025-12-01
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/zanwenfu/svd-lora"
abstract: >-
  We systematically compare three representative low-rank adaptation methods
  (LoRA, Sparse LoRA, and HiRA) on a shared DistilBERT backbone under a
  controlled training protocol, then introduce an SVD-guided adaptive rank
  compression scheme that trains a high-rank LoRA, applies per-module
  truncated SVD at a fixed Frobenius-energy threshold, and fine-tunes in the
  reduced subspace. The compressed adapters use roughly 30% of the original
  parameters while matching or surpassing standard LoRA on SST-2 and IMDB.
keywords:
  - parameter-efficient fine-tuning
  - LoRA
  - low-rank adaptation
  - SVD
  - DistilBERT
  - transformers
